abstract = {In the digital transformation era, modern enterprises face persistent challenges in their internal product-selling models, including high labor costs, inefficient inventory management, and unsatisfactory user experiences. To overcome these issues, this study aims to explore the innovative application of unattended sales technology in corporate environments. It proposes the design and implementation of an internal automated sales management system built upon a “six-core modules + sub-module collaboration” architecture, integrating intelligent product management, unattended identification and pickup, multi-dimensional transaction settlement, real-time inventory synchronization, data-driven analytics, and user interaction feedback. Through this integrated framework, the system effectively resolves traditional pain points such as stock imbalances, recognition errors, and data fragmentation. Practical implementation demonstrates its effectiveness, achieving over 30% reduction in internal management costs, a 25% increase in inventory turnover, and significant improvement in employee shopping experiences. Overall, this research offers not only a viable solution to enhance enterprise sales efficiency but also provides a replicable framework and theoretical foundation for the broader application of unattended sales technologies across diverse corporate settings.},
