abstract = {With the dynamic shifts in population structure, traditional static models for allocating educational resources struggle to meet the demands of precise decision-making. This study leverages deep learning technology to design and implement an intelligent decision support system for allocating vocational education resources. The system employs an LSTM neural network to construct population forecasting models, utilizes a distributed computing framework to execute multi-objective optimization algorithms, and integrates the system through a Spring Boot microservices architecture. Experimental results demonstrate: the system achieved prediction errors controlled between 2-4% using actual data from 16 prefecture-level cities, with concurrent processing capacity optimized by Redis cache reaching 3,200 requests per second. The resource allocation plan elevated educational resource utilization to 87.3%. This research innovatively integrates artificial intelligence with educational resource allocation, enabling intelligent and dynamic configuration decisions. The system's deployment provides regional education authorities with a reliable decision-support tool, offering significant practical value for advancing the digital transformation of educational resource allocation.},
