abstract = {Contemporary rule-of-law education is faced with many challenges, including the complexity of legal concepts and the ambiguity of knowledge connections. This study proposes an AI-based system for teaching the rule of law, integrating knowledge visualisation and intelligent dialogue. The system is designed to visualise legal knowledge networks using force-directed graph algorithms, and to answer questions intelligently using a BERT-BiLSTM-based module. The system establishes a multidimensional legal knowledge representation mechanism and a strategy for generating personalised learning paths. Experimental validation demonstrates the system's significant advantages in enhancing learning outcomes, sustaining knowledge retention and strengthening practical application capabilities. These findings provide a new paradigm for digital rule-of-law education and have significant implications for the precise dissemination and in-depth learning of legal knowledge.},
