abstract = {To enhance the distribution efficiency and service stability of ideological and political education resources, a repository system model based on content delivery network (CDN) technology was constructed. Building upon the traditional centralized resource distribution architecture, this model incorporates multi-level edge node deployment and intelligent scheduling mechanisms. It integrates key technologies such as LVS load balancing, LRFU caching strategy, and hybrid RBAC/ABAC permission control to form a three-tier system structure and dynamic resource adaptation framework. Experimental results demonstrate that compared to traditional systems, average resource loading latency decreased by 588ms, request failure rate dropped by 1.25%, and content synchronization time shortened to 13.2 seconds, validating the model's superior performance under high-concurrency and weak network conditions.},
