abstract = {An advanced deep learning-based quantitative risk analysis system for military equipment development costs is proposed in this study. This research addresses the computational challenges posed by the large amount of multidimensional data generated by complex military projects by developing an intelligent risk analysis framework that integrates a hybrid CNN-LSTM architecture, distributed Monte Carlo simulation, and real-time monitoring capability. The system architecture includes components for intelligent risk identification, high-performance quantization, real-time monitoring, and decision support. Experimental validation on a comprehensive dataset of 258 military projects from 2015-2024 demonstrates the system's superior performance, with a prediction accuracy of 96.8% and a processing speed of 85ms per risk assessment. The results show significant improvements in accuracy, resource utilization, and scalability compared to traditional statistical methods.},
